#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# triangle_wave

#% text
# `triangle_wave(x)` gives the triangle wave of period 1 that is 0 at 0, 1 at 1/4, 0 at 1/2 and -1 at 3/4.

#% text
# `triangle_wave([a, b], x)` gives the same wave between a and b.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is `1 - 4 |s - 1/2|` with `s = sawtooth_wave(x + 1/4)`; exact arguments give exact values.

#% item
# Lists are mapped element-wise; symbolic arguments stay unevaluated. The derivative is `4 square_wave(x + 1/4)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
triangle_wave(0.2)
#% output
#= 0.8

#% cell
table(triangle_wave(x), [x, 0, 1, 1/8])
#% output
#= [0, 1/2, 1, 1/2, 0, -1/2, -1, -1/2, 0]

#% cell
triangle_wave([0, 2], 1.6)
#% output
#= 0.5999999999999996

#% cell
n(triangle_wave(1/47), 30)
#% output
#= 0.08510638297872340425531914893617021

#% cell
d(triangle_wave(x), x)
#% output
#= 4*square_wave(1/4 + x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `square_wave`, `sawtooth_wave`, `heaviside_lambda`, `unit_triangle`
